WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.410
&gt;&gt; Now, let's get into
some serious stuff

00:00:07.411 --> 00:00:09.225
what we wanted to do is

00:00:09.226 --> 00:00:10.965
give you a glimpse of

00:00:10.966 --> 00:00:12.090
the great work that's been

00:00:12.091 --> 00:00:14.295
happening in the social sector.

00:00:14.296 --> 00:00:16.560
We have a series of

00:00:16.561 --> 00:00:20.685
presentations which are
curated specifically

00:00:20.686 --> 00:00:22.860
to give you a context and

00:00:22.861 --> 00:00:27.210
the possible opportunity area
of AI implementation.

00:00:27.211 --> 00:00:29.015
I would like to invite.

00:00:29.016 --> 00:00:32.160
Ms. Shashikala from WWF.

00:00:32.161 --> 00:00:35.500
She could come and
share her thoughts.

00:00:35.501 --> 00:00:37.975
&gt;&gt; Good afternoon
everyone I'm Shashikala.

00:00:37.976 --> 00:00:39.900
I'm from WWF- India,

00:00:39.901 --> 00:00:41.635
Worldwide Fund for Nature.

00:00:41.636 --> 00:00:46.640
It's an NGO that works for
wildlife conservation.

00:00:46.641 --> 00:00:49.310
It started as wildlife
conservation organization

00:00:49.311 --> 00:00:52.425
but we are now working
on varied fields.

00:00:52.426 --> 00:00:55.745
So, basically, our aim is
to stop the degradation

00:00:55.746 --> 00:00:58.640
of natural resources and

00:00:58.641 --> 00:01:01.420
man lives in harmony with nature.

00:01:01.421 --> 00:01:05.950
So, that's the basic concept
in which WWF works.

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:09.330
We were founded in 1969

00:01:09.331 --> 00:01:12.600
and in India this
is our 50th year.

00:01:12.601 --> 00:01:15.950
So, we have our offices in I

00:01:15.951 --> 00:01:19.280
think more than 20
states in India,

00:01:19.281 --> 00:01:22.105
and we have different
project offices as well.

00:01:22.106 --> 00:01:24.890
In Karnataka we
started working in

00:01:24.891 --> 00:01:28.730
this wetland division
from last five years,

00:01:28.731 --> 00:01:33.320
and we have start try
to bring about changes.

00:01:33.321 --> 00:01:35.640
We started with like
rural areas more.

00:01:35.641 --> 00:01:38.075
So we started in
wetland conservation

00:01:38.076 --> 00:01:40.835
in some areas which
are like peri-urban,

00:01:40.836 --> 00:01:42.725
not fully urban areas.

00:01:42.726 --> 00:01:46.070
But this year, we have
started with urban also.

00:01:46.071 --> 00:01:49.265
So, until or unless
we touch urban areas,

00:01:49.266 --> 00:01:51.370
it doesn't show much.

00:01:51.371 --> 00:01:55.660
So, we have done lot of
work and whenever we do,

00:01:55.661 --> 00:01:58.155
we think that
stakeholder participation,

00:01:58.156 --> 00:01:59.855
community participation

00:01:59.856 --> 00:02:02.000
and all these things
are very important.

00:02:02.001 --> 00:02:06.195
But lately, we have got
to know that technology

00:02:06.196 --> 00:02:08.060
also helps a lot in

00:02:08.061 --> 00:02:11.300
wetland conservation and all the
conservation activities,

00:02:11.301 --> 00:02:14.650
like social, whatever social
activities you want to do.

00:02:14.651 --> 00:02:17.330
So, technology can play
a very important rule and

00:02:17.331 --> 00:02:20.275
we have felt it many
ways, many times.

00:02:20.276 --> 00:02:23.780
So, these are the places

00:02:23.781 --> 00:02:25.735
where we are working
in Karnataka.

00:02:25.736 --> 00:02:29.095
So, one is Madiwala Wetland.

00:02:29.096 --> 00:02:31.020
If somebody's from Bangalore,

00:02:31.021 --> 00:02:33.120
they might have
visited this place.

00:02:33.121 --> 00:02:34.520
It's in BTM layout,

00:02:34.521 --> 00:02:35.985
it in South Bangalore.

00:02:35.986 --> 00:02:39.345
So, that's a pretty
good wetland to visit.

00:02:39.346 --> 00:02:42.080
Then, we have Kokkarebellur down,

00:02:42.081 --> 00:02:45.050
so it is on the way to Mysuru.

00:02:45.051 --> 00:02:46.580
When you go to Mysuru,

00:02:46.581 --> 00:02:49.210
many of you must have
visited Ranganathittu.

00:02:49.211 --> 00:02:51.780
Somebody has visited
Ranganathittu?

00:02:51.781 --> 00:02:53.480
Yeah. So, Ranganathittu, but

00:02:53.481 --> 00:02:55.440
nobody must have
visited Kokkarebellur.

00:02:55.441 --> 00:02:58.020
Anybody? Okay. Great. I have

00:02:58.021 --> 00:02:59.860
two people who have
visited Kokkarebellur.

00:02:59.861 --> 00:03:02.510
So, the best part of
Kokkarebellur is it

00:03:02.511 --> 00:03:05.865
is the only community
reserve in Karnataka.

00:03:05.866 --> 00:03:08.735
So, what does a
community reserve?

00:03:08.736 --> 00:03:11.645
A community reserve
is a place where

00:03:11.646 --> 00:03:16.020
the village or the place
which is all protected.

00:03:16.021 --> 00:03:18.385
So, the villagers
protected in itself.

00:03:18.386 --> 00:03:21.035
So, the birds come
there for nesting.

00:03:21.036 --> 00:03:24.140
So, every season, we
see like thousands

00:03:24.141 --> 00:03:25.850
of pelicans and printed storks

00:03:25.851 --> 00:03:27.845
coming from Southeast Asia.

00:03:27.846 --> 00:03:30.800
They come inside
the village and they stay

00:03:30.801 --> 00:03:33.380
there for a good two
to three months,

00:03:33.381 --> 00:03:34.940
and they give birth to

00:03:34.941 --> 00:03:37.260
their offsprings and then
they take them back.

00:03:37.261 --> 00:03:38.735
So, that is how it is.

00:03:38.736 --> 00:03:43.005
You can see on the nests
like just you,

00:03:43.006 --> 00:03:44.690
if you go and stand there and

00:03:44.691 --> 00:03:46.630
that's like a beautiful
sight to see.

00:03:46.631 --> 00:03:50.870
The people there they are
so used to this that they

00:03:50.871 --> 00:03:55.680
will never lit firecrackers
during Diwali,

00:03:55.681 --> 00:03:58.680
because they say that it
will scare the birds.

00:03:58.681 --> 00:04:00.710
Even the kids there
don't do that,

00:04:00.711 --> 00:04:02.000
so that is something which is

00:04:02.001 --> 00:04:03.825
like we have to learn from them.

00:04:03.826 --> 00:04:05.585
So, that is the way of life,

00:04:05.586 --> 00:04:07.610
they will never build
a second story in

00:04:07.611 --> 00:04:08.960
their houses because they see in

00:04:08.961 --> 00:04:11.020
a second story birds live there.

00:04:11.021 --> 00:04:13.200
We don't have to build
our second story.

00:04:13.201 --> 00:04:17.330
So, they are all in
sync with nature.

00:04:17.331 --> 00:04:20.025
So, that's very important
about Kokkarebellur.

00:04:20.026 --> 00:04:22.550
In Kunigal, Kunigal
is one more place

00:04:22.551 --> 00:04:25.740
where it is attached to a town,

00:04:25.741 --> 00:04:28.775
Kunigal town and Kunigal
don't decorate the sea,

00:04:28.776 --> 00:04:31.025
it's so big lake, big wetland.

00:04:31.026 --> 00:04:36.225
So, drinking water is supplied
to few of Kunigal place.

00:04:36.226 --> 00:04:40.075
Then, we have Bashettihalli
wetland which is

00:04:40.076 --> 00:04:45.385
ahead of Bangalore International
Airport in [inaudible] Town.

00:04:45.386 --> 00:04:47.495
So there is a [inaudible] park,

00:04:47.496 --> 00:04:49.655
it's in [inaudible]
industrial area.

00:04:49.656 --> 00:04:52.490
So, it is like a very typical of

00:04:52.491 --> 00:04:55.730
a wetland because one side
you have Industries,

00:04:55.731 --> 00:04:58.745
one side you have a village.

00:04:58.746 --> 00:05:02.030
To bring both of them
together for conservation is

00:05:02.031 --> 00:05:06.015
a victim because industry
say that villagers,

00:05:06.016 --> 00:05:07.895
they don't understand and they

00:05:07.896 --> 00:05:10.235
throw their garbage inside.

00:05:10.236 --> 00:05:12.260
Villager will say that they are

00:05:12.261 --> 00:05:14.855
discharging their effluent
into the lake.

00:05:14.856 --> 00:05:17.095
So, that's a victim.
So, today I'm

00:05:17.096 --> 00:05:21.010
just concentrating on
Bashetihalli Wetland.

00:05:22.910 --> 00:05:27.619
So, Bashetihalli Wetland if
you see, the major threats,

00:05:27.620 --> 00:05:30.190
whenever we start
any intervention in

00:05:30.191 --> 00:05:33.365
any place we suppose to do
the situation analysis.

00:05:33.366 --> 00:05:35.235
We go around, we
talked to people.

00:05:35.236 --> 00:05:39.200
We do all the maps, we see
what all is the major issues.

00:05:39.201 --> 00:05:42.430
Then, we got these other threats

00:05:42.431 --> 00:05:45.740
which we found like connectivity
with cascade tanks.

00:05:45.741 --> 00:05:48.990
So, if you see in Bangalor,

00:05:48.991 --> 00:05:51.085
e as well as in Karnataka,

00:05:51.086 --> 00:05:54.085
all the wetlands are
cascade systems.

00:05:54.086 --> 00:05:56.170
So, if you touch one wetland,

00:05:56.171 --> 00:05:57.760
there will be like two wetlands

00:05:57.761 --> 00:05:59.695
above, two wetlands below.

00:05:59.696 --> 00:06:01.230
So, you have to look at

00:06:01.231 --> 00:06:05.090
the wetland series, not
individual wetland.

00:06:05.091 --> 00:06:06.380
That's what we did,

00:06:06.381 --> 00:06:09.275
we did a lot of surveys
with the local people

00:06:09.276 --> 00:06:12.400
as well as the agencies.
There are many agencies.

00:06:12.401 --> 00:06:13.630
There are KIADB, there are

00:06:13.631 --> 00:06:15.865
KSPCB, Pollution Control Board.

00:06:15.866 --> 00:06:17.930
So, we did the survey to find

00:06:17.931 --> 00:06:19.880
out what are the channels which

00:06:19.881 --> 00:06:21.990
bring water into this wetland

00:06:21.991 --> 00:06:24.170
and why the water is
not coming into it.

00:06:24.171 --> 00:06:26.630
So, that was a major concern
because this lake,

00:06:26.631 --> 00:06:28.340
the major concern
is this wetland.

00:06:28.341 --> 00:06:30.920
Water is not coming
into it because

00:06:30.921 --> 00:06:33.510
the catchment area
is fully developed.

00:06:33.511 --> 00:06:35.975
There is no space for
water to come inside.

00:06:35.976 --> 00:06:37.340
So, then we said, "Okay.

00:06:37.341 --> 00:06:40.310
If the water is not coming
from the catchment area,

00:06:40.311 --> 00:06:42.635
let us at least rejuvenate

00:06:42.636 --> 00:06:45.750
the channels which can
bring the water into."

00:06:45.751 --> 00:06:47.600
So, when we started doing that,

00:06:47.601 --> 00:06:52.485
we did the GIS and we
did all the survey.

00:06:52.486 --> 00:06:55.250
We saw the blockages,
like blockages there.

00:06:55.251 --> 00:06:59.510
So we took the GIS from
there and we put it in

00:06:59.511 --> 00:07:01.580
the map and we saw like how it is

00:07:01.581 --> 00:07:04.520
blocked and you have to
desilt it or whatever.

00:07:04.521 --> 00:07:07.430
So, again, we use
some technology for

00:07:07.431 --> 00:07:10.655
that and we got
a pretty okay map of that.

00:07:10.656 --> 00:07:12.570
So, over abstraction of

00:07:12.571 --> 00:07:16.220
groundwater because there is
no water in that wetland.

00:07:16.221 --> 00:07:19.815
And there is no other major
source of water there.

00:07:19.816 --> 00:07:22.655
So, the people around
and the industries,

00:07:22.656 --> 00:07:24.880
they are extracting
groundwater and

00:07:24.881 --> 00:07:27.350
the groundwater has become
a major business there.

00:07:27.351 --> 00:07:29.870
So, whenever you go and
stand there you will see

00:07:29.871 --> 00:07:32.495
like 10 tankers going everywhere.

00:07:32.496 --> 00:07:33.890
So, it's like common because

00:07:33.891 --> 00:07:35.745
industries they can't
live without water.

00:07:35.746 --> 00:07:38.090
They need water but
they don't have water.

00:07:38.091 --> 00:07:39.950
So, they have to pay a big price

00:07:39.951 --> 00:07:42.865
and that's the reason
when we spoke to

00:07:42.866 --> 00:07:45.370
many of these industries
they were like please

00:07:45.371 --> 00:07:48.005
we will help you in
rejuvenating this wetland.

00:07:48.006 --> 00:07:49.400
At least we'll get water

00:07:49.401 --> 00:07:51.535
without paying
hefty sum of money.

00:07:51.536 --> 00:07:53.790
So, that was something
which we got

00:07:53.791 --> 00:07:56.175
it from there and in
Bashettihalli yeah.

00:07:56.176 --> 00:07:59.220
So, we never thought
that we will get

00:07:59.221 --> 00:08:03.015
to see birds in
such a degraded wetland.

00:08:03.016 --> 00:08:05.180
We never thought when we started.

00:08:05.181 --> 00:08:07.645
Then we started doing surveys,

00:08:07.646 --> 00:08:11.310
and we saw like pelicans

00:08:11.311 --> 00:08:15.120
painted stocks and good number
of like around 44 birds.

00:08:15.121 --> 00:08:17.350
We have already documented

00:08:17.351 --> 00:08:20.120
44 species of birds
in Bashettihalli,

00:08:20.121 --> 00:08:22.910
and that's a good thing for
such a degraded wetland.

00:08:22.911 --> 00:08:27.625
So, if it has water so it can
have like 100 or 140 birds.

00:08:27.626 --> 00:08:29.805
Then solid waste dumping
is one more thing

00:08:29.806 --> 00:08:31.930
because we have seen in

00:08:31.931 --> 00:08:34.700
everywhere even in
urban area if you see,

00:08:34.701 --> 00:08:36.120
whenever we see a land

00:08:36.121 --> 00:08:38.200
where no water is there
nothing is there,

00:08:38.201 --> 00:08:41.325
people will start making
it a garbage dumping area.

00:08:41.326 --> 00:08:43.095
So, that was what was happening.

00:08:43.096 --> 00:08:46.490
So, we started with bringing

00:08:46.491 --> 00:08:48.860
all the stakeholders
together and forming

00:08:48.861 --> 00:08:51.470
a committee and talking to them.

00:08:51.471 --> 00:08:54.040
So, in WWF we have a thing

00:08:54.041 --> 00:08:57.180
that whenever we leave

00:08:57.181 --> 00:09:00.040
a project it should
be sustainable.

00:09:00.041 --> 00:09:02.425
It's not like
three years we are there

00:09:02.426 --> 00:09:06.535
and we will do A B C
D things then once we leave,

00:09:06.536 --> 00:09:07.910
there is nothing for them to do

00:09:07.911 --> 00:09:09.575
and people don't know what to do.

00:09:09.576 --> 00:09:12.415
So, we make a committee
of all the stakeholders.

00:09:12.416 --> 00:09:14.925
It includes local people and

00:09:14.926 --> 00:09:16.450
all the agencies and

00:09:16.451 --> 00:09:18.855
NGOs if some NGOs
are working around.

00:09:18.856 --> 00:09:22.275
So, we bring those people
also and then we

00:09:22.276 --> 00:09:23.765
talk to them and

00:09:23.766 --> 00:09:25.880
then we'll make
a management action plan.

00:09:25.881 --> 00:09:28.200
We need to do A B C D things.

00:09:28.201 --> 00:09:29.865
Then the people there will tell,

00:09:29.866 --> 00:09:32.580
no I think C is more
important than A.

00:09:32.581 --> 00:09:34.880
So, if C is more
important than A,

00:09:34.881 --> 00:09:36.770
then let us start with C. So,

00:09:36.771 --> 00:09:38.100
that's how we do it.

00:09:38.101 --> 00:09:40.325
So, once it's done,

00:09:40.326 --> 00:09:43.600
so people take ownership
of that activity.

00:09:43.601 --> 00:09:45.340
Like, oh, I was only the person

00:09:45.341 --> 00:09:47.280
who asked them to do this and

00:09:47.281 --> 00:09:51.090
see this has given results.

00:09:51.091 --> 00:09:54.850
So that way, we have started
working there and now we

00:09:54.851 --> 00:09:58.680
are trying to join
the cascade of wetlands.

00:09:58.681 --> 00:10:01.110
There are like five or
six via cascade wetlands.

00:10:01.111 --> 00:10:05.670
So, we are trying to join it
so that water flows into it.

00:10:08.290 --> 00:10:10.940
So, we had developed

00:10:10.941 --> 00:10:14.045
one more concept of
wetland health assessment.

00:10:14.046 --> 00:10:16.460
So, wherever we start working we

00:10:16.461 --> 00:10:19.475
will start with wetland
health assessment.

00:10:19.476 --> 00:10:22.940
So, this is important
because we have to see

00:10:22.941 --> 00:10:27.655
wetlands as holistically
ecological.

00:10:27.656 --> 00:10:31.165
So, when we see that we
see the catchment health,

00:10:31.166 --> 00:10:34.120
then community perception,
water quality,

00:10:34.121 --> 00:10:35.800
and then biota health.

00:10:35.801 --> 00:10:38.900
So, community perceptions
many places when we see

00:10:38.901 --> 00:10:42.080
there is no use of this,

00:10:42.081 --> 00:10:44.795
like now this water body
this is just there.

00:10:44.796 --> 00:10:47.745
We don't know if it
is useful or not.

00:10:47.746 --> 00:10:49.225
Then we'll tell them okay,

00:10:49.226 --> 00:10:51.700
you have a ground bore
well in your house.

00:10:51.701 --> 00:10:53.340
Let's see where we
have a bore well.

00:10:53.341 --> 00:10:56.740
Okay so, 20 years back
what was they're like no.

00:10:56.741 --> 00:10:58.900
So, they'll say 20 years
back we used to

00:10:58.901 --> 00:11:00.990
get elected 500 meters of water.

00:11:00.991 --> 00:11:03.200
So, now it's 1,200.

00:11:03.201 --> 00:11:04.430
So, why this is happening?

00:11:04.431 --> 00:11:05.575
Because water is not there.

00:11:05.576 --> 00:11:07.660
So, water table is not
getting recharged.

00:11:07.661 --> 00:11:10.345
Those things they
were like oh yes,

00:11:10.346 --> 00:11:13.565
so this is important
for me to sustain?

00:11:13.566 --> 00:11:16.230
So those things come into
community perception.

00:11:16.231 --> 00:11:18.570
So we have a survey form which

00:11:18.571 --> 00:11:21.675
we go and talk to people
and we tell them,

00:11:21.676 --> 00:11:24.230
how do you perceive this wetland?

00:11:24.231 --> 00:11:26.705
How would this wetland
is important?

00:11:26.706 --> 00:11:29.360
Even if it is important
for you or not.

00:11:29.361 --> 00:11:31.030
So, many of them will say, no no.

00:11:31.031 --> 00:11:33.600
I don't think there's
nothing in this wetland.

00:11:33.601 --> 00:11:36.365
This is just mosquito
breeding ground or whatever.

00:11:36.366 --> 00:11:38.150
So, we get different type of

00:11:38.151 --> 00:11:40.660
perception of people.
Then Catchment health.

00:11:40.661 --> 00:11:42.910
Definitely Catchment health
we go around and

00:11:42.911 --> 00:11:45.650
see if it's full

00:11:45.651 --> 00:11:48.180
constructed or fully be graded or

00:11:48.181 --> 00:11:51.085
there is chance of
bringing it back.

00:11:51.086 --> 00:11:52.570
Then water quality.

00:11:52.571 --> 00:11:55.590
So, we do it like water analysis.

00:11:55.591 --> 00:11:57.695
We have like easy to use kit.

00:11:57.696 --> 00:12:02.825
So, we can have like 14 15
parameters at a single go.

00:12:02.826 --> 00:12:05.540
So, we take that
parameters like take

00:12:05.541 --> 00:12:09.645
that box and we do the 15
parameters and we get the,

00:12:09.646 --> 00:12:13.415
we can't get the accurate
in that easy-to-use kit,

00:12:13.416 --> 00:12:14.960
but yes, we get the approx.

00:12:14.961 --> 00:12:17.130
Like no no, how much
is ammonia content or

00:12:17.131 --> 00:12:18.580
how much nitrogen or

00:12:18.581 --> 00:12:20.610
dissolved oxygen or
things like that?

00:12:20.611 --> 00:12:22.220
So, we'll get an idea

00:12:22.221 --> 00:12:24.050
and then biota health
and definitely,

00:12:24.051 --> 00:12:25.430
we'll see like birds,

00:12:25.431 --> 00:12:29.240
water birds are seen or
